/ solution design / requirements\n* not “runtime” → delivery process / implementation cadence\n* not “state” → current project status / current assumptions\n* not “governance substrate” → project governance / decision process / escalation\n* not “routing” → workstream ownership / specialist handoff\n* not “convergence” → reconcile findings / align stakeholders / resolve open decisions\n\nAnd the new open research item for tomorrow is very specific:\n\nMap the Myers-Holum pre-sales → delivery seam.\n\nWe need to understand:\n\n1. What their pre-sales / solution architecture team actually owns.\n2. What they likely hand a Principal Consultant after the deal closes.\n3. What is already decided versus what the Principal is expected to validate.\n4. How SuiteSuccess fits into that handoff.\n5. What MHI calls the actual documents/process — SOW, solution design, requirements, project charter, implementation plan, etc.\n6. Where your responsibility starts.\n\nThat matters because your existing Drive language says “pressure-test what NetSuite sold and what Myers-Holum inherited.” Based on what Jillian told you, that may be slightly wrong for this interview. MHI may be originating/scoping a meaningful portion of the sale themselves. Tomorrow we should correct that from “what NetSuite sold” to something closer to:\n\n“validate the sold scope and pre-sales solution before delivery begins.”\n\nThat removes an assumption without changing the principle.\n\nSo the handoff into the new chat is clean:\n\nExisting Drive framework = source material.\nTomorrow = simplify to the six-lane command board, build the proof bank, and research the MHI pre-sales handoff so we understand exactly what lands on Peter’s desk.\n\nThat’s the anchor."]}, "create_time": 1789361918.382951, "end_turn": null, "id": "75d8b95e-a6b0-40c4-a9fe-c7aef220e6b8", "metadata": {"can_save": false, "dictation": false, "message_source": null, "request_id": "f94ee175-292f-49b9-ae26-cd8757ee6266", "triggered_by_system_hin