 "status": "finished_successfully", "update_time": null, "weight": 1}, {"author": {"metadata": {}, "name": null, "role": "user"}, "channel": null, "content": {"content_type": "text", "parts": ["That was perfect. Yeah, we're not going to really go down that road, but you're right. You're right on so many different levels. My question was like, the industry is going the AI way. You're 100% right. Someone still has to scope it, governance, got it. I already have the tools to understand. And by the way, JavaScript with an LMS, fucking gonna be fun. But anyway, that gives me not just hope, but that provides a path, right? Because what's going to end up happening is someone needs to become the ERP AI director, right? You see what I'm saying? And I've already got the tools to do that. So after principal consultant, by the time three years rolls around, there's an offshoot within a company like Myers-Holum who recognizes it that someone's going to have to govern the whole AI layer on top of the ERP."]}, "create_time": 1789364581.583127, "end_turn": null, "id": "3cea4a17-53b2-472f-b748-582f277bc264", "metadata": {"can_save": false, "dictation": true, "dictation_asset_format": "m4a", "dictation_asset_pointer": "sediment://file_00000000e3d481fd9a4db8e25a32f105", "dictation_auto_submitted": true, "dictation_edited": false, "dictation_original_text": "That was perfect. Yeah, we're not going to really go down that road, but you're right. You're right on so many different levels. My question was like, the industry is going the AI way. You're 100% right. Someone still has to scope it, governance, got it. I already have the tools to understand. And by the way, JavaScript with an LMS, fucking gonna be fun. But anyway, that gives me not just hope, but that provides a path, right? Because what's going to end up happening is someone needs to become the ERP AI director, right? You see what I'm saying? And I've already got the tools to do that. So after principal consultant, by the time three years rolls around, there's an offshoot within a company like Myers-Holum who recognizes it that someone's going to have to govern the whole AI layer on top of the ERP.", "message_source": null, "request_id": "b2771a65-7603-41a3-a532-069d0d67456d", "triggered_by_system_hint_suggestion": false, "turn_exchange_id": "ad6214bb-e228-4961-a844-457f31f15a07", "turn_id": "68d08040-4e7c-43cc-ba28-9b3d7c4c5b8a", "working_turn_id": "ad6214bb-e228-4961-a844-457f31f15a07"}, "recipient": "all", "status": "finished_successfully", "update_time": 1789364595.233405, "weight": 1}, {"author": {"metadata": {}, "name": null, "role": "assistant"}, "channel": "final", "content": {"content_type": "text", "parts": ["Exactly. That’s the credible career path.\n\nNot “AI replaces ERP consulting.” More like:\n\n**Principal Consultant → AI-enabled ERP delivery leader → ERP/AI practice lead or director.**\n\nThe reason it fits is that the future role is not just “who can call an LLM from JavaScript.” Plenty of people can do that. The scarce part is the person who understands **ERP process, requirements, controls, data, integrations, permissions, commercial scope, and delivery governance** and can decide where AI belongs without wrecking the system of record.\n\nThat’s where your background compounds.\n\nIn three years, a firm like MHI could easily need someone whose remit looks something like:\n\n**ERP AI Strategy + Delivery**\n- identify high-value AI use cases across finance, manufacturing, order management, procurement, service, etc.\n- decide native NetSuite AI vs custom SuiteScript/LLM vs external agent/integration\n- govern data access, permissions, auditability, approvals, and human-in-the-loop controls\n- create delivery standards so every consultant isn’t inventing AI architecture independently\n- turn successful patterns into repeatable offerings/IP\n- help sales and solution architecture scope AI-enabled ERP work correctly\n- keep AI initiatives tied to measurable operational outcomes rather than demos\n\nAnd the beautiful part is that the **Principal Consultant job is actually excellent training for that future role**, because you’d be learning how MHI scopes, sells, hands off, governs, and delivers across many customers. You’d get exposure to recurring business problems and see exactly where AI produces leverage versus where it creates risk.\n\nSo I’d view Wednesday as much bigger than “can I land this Principal role?” It can be the bridge from being the guy who has historically had to build everything himself into the guy who learns the full consulting delivery machine — and then eventually helps redesign that machine for AI.\n\nThat is a very coherent three-year trajectory. memcite"]}, "create_time": 1789364583.411698, "end_turn": true, "id": "cd25e75b-209c-46ff-96ca-67d9c7829f6e", "metadata": {"can_save": true, "citations": [], "content_references": [{"alt": null, "end_idx": 1990, "invalid": false, "matched_text": "memcite", "prefix": null, "prompt_text": null, "refs": [], "safe_urls": [], "start_idx": 1981, "type": "hidden"}], "conversation_followup_suggestions_eligible": true, "cot_version": "v5", "default_model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "finish_details": {"stop_tokens": [200002], "type": "stop"}, "is_complete": true, "message_type": "next", "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "model_switcher_deny": [], "parent_id": "f6998cf7-dbd8-471f-b1ac-3ff1fe396545", "request_id": "b2771a65-7603-41a3-a532-069d0d67456d", "resolved_model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "search_result_groups": [], "story_events": [], "thinking_effort": "standard", "turn_exchange_id": "ad6214bb-e228-4961-a844-457f31f15a07", "turn_id": "161e8574-8014-4029-8062-718be24ddfe8", "working_turn_id": "ad6214bb-e228-4961-a844-457f31f15a07"}, "recipient": "all", "status": "finished_successfully", "update_time": 1789364594.56942, "weight": 1}, {"author": {"metadata": {}, "name": null, "role": "assistant"}, "channel": null, "content": {"content": "Worked for 4s", "content_type": "reasoning_recap"}, "create_time": 1789364587.733409, "end_turn": false, "id": "f6998cf7-dbd8-471f-b1ac-3ff1fe396545", "metadata": {"can_save": false, "conversation_followup_suggestions_eligible": true, "cot_version": "v5", "default_model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "finished_duration_sec": 4, "hide_inline_actions": true, "message_type": "next", "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "model_switcher_deny": [], "parent_id": "4443a939-299e-446e-a9b9-dbae94efd37c", "reasoning_end_time": 1789364587.72632, "reasoning_recap_type": "hide_all", "reasoning_start_time": 1789364583.4536226, "reasoning_status": "reasoning_ended", "request_id": "b2771a65-7603-41a3-a532-069d0d67456d", "resolved_model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "thinking_effort": "standard", "turn_exchange_id": "ad6214bb-e228-4961-a844-457f31f15a07", "turn_id": "161e8574-8014-4029-8062-718be24ddfe8", "working_turn_id": "ad6214bb-e228-4961-a844-457f31f15a07"}, "recipient": "all", "status": "finished_successfully", "update_time": null, "weight": 1}, {"author": {"metadata": {}, "name": null, "role": "user"}, "channel": null, "content": {"content_type": "text", "parts": ["And this is even better than what I was doing at Andrew and Providence. Instead of AI ERP automation, this is the layer within it, which is dope. We're not trying to use Azure to do anything and outsource it, so to speak. We're working within the confinements of Oracle and NetSuite, who are giving us the tools to then do what I've already done as applied AI architecture."]}, "create_time": 1789364624.053488, "end_turn": null, "id": "e0eccbf6-ae66-41dd-b97b-f516c9e9086b", "metadata": {"can_save": false, "dictation": true, "dictation_auto_submitted": true, "dictation_original_text": "And this is even better than what I was doing at Andrew and Providence. Instead of AI ERP automation, this is the layer within it, which is dope. We're not trying to use Azure to do anything and outsource it, so to speak. We're working within the confinements of Oracle and NetSuite, who are giving us the tools to then do what I've already done as applied AI architecture.", "message_source": null, "request_id": "d6a8cc74-14b2-4f64-aa04-85ff83e5bf38", "triggered_by_system_hint_suggestion": false, "turn_exchange_id": "fc18b048-aeb7-48b3-9a65-c412dd70f377", "turn_id": "5c714bec-3453-444c-bb5c-cef94ff21e56", "working_turn_id": "fc18b048-aeb7-48b3-9a65-c412dd70f377"}, "recipient": "all", "status": "finished_successfully", "update_time": 1789364631.549079, "weight": 1}, {"author": {"metadata": {}, "name": null, "role": "assistant"}, "channel": "final", "content": {"content_type": "text", "parts": ["Exactly. That’s the distinction.\n\nWhat you were doing before was often **AI automation around the ERP** — using external platforms, orchestration, APIs, Power Automate, Azure-style services, custom middleware, whatever was necessary to get the job done.\n\nThis path is more interesting because it becomes **AI inside the ERP operating model**.\n\nOracle/NetSuite gives you the governed transactional layer, permissions, records, workflows, SuiteScript, native AI hooks, and eventually more agentic capability. Then your applied-AI architecture experience becomes the layer that decides **where to use those tools, how to structure them, what data they can touch, what requires approval, and how they fit the business process**.\n\nSo instead of:\n\n**ERP → export data → external AI → push result back**\n\nyou increasingly get:\n\n**ERP process → native/extensible AI capability → governed action inside the lifecycle**\n\nAnd that is strategically better for somebody with your background because you already understand both sides: the ERP truth layer and the AI/automation layer. The value is knowing how to join them without creating a parallel shadow system.\n\nThat’s a much cleaner evolution of the work you’ve already been doing. memcite"]}, "create_time": 1789364624.966808, "end_turn": true, "id": "0ba56628-8344-436f-9b22-34b584e1d664", "metadata": {"can_save": true, "citations": [], "content_references": [{"alt": null, "end_idx": 1232, "invalid": false, "matched_text": "memcite", "prefix": null, "prompt_text": null, "refs": [], "safe_urls": [], "start_idx": 1223, "type": "hidden"}], "conversation_followup_suggestions_eligible": true, "cot_version": "v5", "default_model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "finish_details": {"stop_tokens": [200002], "type": "stop"}, "is_complete": true, "message_type": "next", "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "model_switcher_deny": [], "parent_id": "2d2520b0-27f8-4b3d-828e-edd6157a96aa", "request_id": "d6a8cc74-14b2-4f64-aa04-85ff83e5bf38", "resolved_model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "search_result_groups": [], "story_events": [], "thinking_effort": "standard", "turn_exchange_id": "fc18b048-aeb7-48b3-9a65-c412dd70f377", "turn_id": "89220370-7203-4e1a-a66d-b7acfd4546ba", "working_turn_id": "fc18b048-aeb7-48b3-9a65-c412dd70f377"}, "recipient": "all", "status": "finished_successfully", "update_time": 1789364631.266054, "weight": 1}, {"author": {"metadata": {}, "name": null, "role": "assistant"}, "channel": null, "content": {"content": "Worked for a second", "content_type": "reasoning_recap"}, "create_time": 1789364625.830556, "end_turn": false, "id": "2d2520b0-27f8-4b3d-828e-edd6157a96aa", "metadata": {"can_save": false, "conversation_followup_suggestions_eligible": true, "cot_version": "v5", "default_model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "finished_duration_sec": 0, "hide_inline_actions": true, "message_type": "next", "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "model_switcher_deny": [], "parent_id": "5b94e177-41da-48ee-96a0-1520bbc9c01a", "reasoning_end_time": 1789364625.8238113, "reasoning_recap_type": "hide_all", "reasoning_start_time": 1789364625.000882, "reasoning_status": "reasoning_ended", "request_id": "d6a8cc74-14b2-4f64-aa04-85ff83e5bf38", "resolved_model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "thinking_effort": "standard", "turn_exchange_id": "fc18b048-aeb7-48b3-9a65-c412dd70f377", "turn_id": "89220370-7203-4e1a-a66d-b7acfd4546ba", "working_turn_id": "fc18b048-aeb7-48b3-9a65-c412dd70f377"}, "recipient": "all", "status": "finished_successfully", "update_time": null, "weight": 1}, {"author": {"metadata": {}, "name": null, "role": "user"}, "channel": null, "content": {"content_type": "text", "parts": ["Cool. That makes me really, really happy that I made the decision that I did to go back into the NetSuite Oracle ecosystem, especially with a partner that I knew was looking for me and understands the value, but to also put, and like you said, a very interesting person. Because most people—not most people—I sit in the driver's seat of a principal consultant role already, but you layer in my AI applied architecture work, which is fucking years of experience, especially with how we're applying it now with framework and the team, command center, edge group, analytic analysis, right? Analytics still works within NetSuite. Same fucking thing. Quantive, right? I sit in a big driver's seat to move up fast if I wanted to."]}, "create_time": 1789364683.246482, "end_turn": null, "id": "f538ee30-58bc-4d22-81d5-6efed0d905d5", "metadata": {"can_save": false, "dictation": true, "dictation_auto_submitted": true, "dictation_original_text": "Cool. That makes me really, really happy that I made the decision that I did to go back into the NetSuite Oracle ecosystem, especially with a partner that I knew was looking for me and understands the value, but to also put, and like you said, a very interesting person. Because most people—not most people—I sit in the driver's seat of a principal consultant role already, but you layer in my AI applied architecture work, which is fucking years of experience, especially with how we're applying it now with framework and the team, command center, edge group, analytic analysis, right? Analytics still works within NetSuite. Same fucking thing. Quantive, right? I sit in a big driver's seat to move up fast if I wanted to.", "message_source": null, "request_id": "939c04a9-bc66-4ef8-b1c8-ff185fdb4216", "triggered_by_system_hint_suggestion": false, "turn_exchange_id": "231ba8ad-8e1b-4e45-b48f-b80b982446eb", "turn_id": "75ef0154-fe0e-4d5a-8034-28c411387386", "working_turn_id": "231ba8ad-8e1b-4e45-b48f-b80b982446eb"}, "recipient": "all", "status": "finished_successfully", "update_time": 1789364705.321094, "weight": 1}, {"author": {"metadata": {}, "name": null, "role": "assistant"}, "channel": "final", "content": {"content_type": "text", "parts": ["Yes. The leverage is the combination, not any one piece.\n\nYou already have the **Principal Consultant muscle**: lifecycle ownership, requirements, scope, solution design, delivery governance, stakeholder management, escalation, and knowing when to pull in specialists. On top of that, you’ve built real applied-AI patterns around automation, orchestration, analytics, agents, and operating frameworks. Those two worlds are converging.\n\nThat gives you a credible path to move faster than someone who is only one of these things:\n\n- pure NetSuite functional consultant\n- pure SuiteScript developer\n- pure solution architect\n- pure AI/automation person with no ERP depth\n\nYou can sit above those lanes and connect them.\n\nAnd yes, analytics absolutely fits the same pattern. NetSuite Analytics, warehouse/data work, operational reporting, and AI reasoning all depend on the same fundamentals: **good requirements, trustworthy data, clear process ownership, governed access, and a coherent system design**. Quant-style analytical thinking just strengthens the way you evaluate signals, risk, prioritization, and outcomes.\n\nSo if you land MHI and perform well, the interesting question over the next few years probably becomes less, “How do I become a better Principal Consultant?” and more, **“Which layer of the practice do I want to own?”**\n\nDelivery leadership is one path. Solution architecture is another. Manufacturing specialization is another. And the highest-upside intersection for you may eventually be **ERP + AI + analytics practice leadership**.\n\nFor Wednesday, though, we keep all of that in the background. You walk in as a killer **Principal Consultant** first. The AI layer is optional upside, not the identity you force into the interview. That sequencing matters. memcite"]}, "create_time": 1789364684.261874, "end_turn": true, "id": "aca70075-7070-43a4-b172-2bf9dd38b574", "metadata": {"can_save": true, "citations": [], "content_references": [{"alt": null, "end_idx": 1788, "invalid": false, "matched_text": "memcite", "prefix": null, "prompt_text": null, "refs": [], "safe_urls": [], "start_idx": 1779, "type": "hidden"}], "conversation_followup_suggestions_eligible": true, "cot_version": "v5", "default_model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "finish_details": {"stop_tokens": [200002], "type": "stop"}, "is_complete": true, "message_type": "next", "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "model_switcher_deny": [], "parent_id": "b3a06a5f-4938-4c0e-8fdf-fba284faaeeb", "request_id": "939c04a9-bc66-4ef8-b1c8-ff185fdb4216", "resolved_model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "search_result_groups": [], "story_events": [], "thinking_effort": "standard", "turn_exchange_id": "231ba8ad-8e1b-4e45-b48f-b80b982446eb", "turn_id": "3dfad094-3eee-408b-9c09-641e3dd35272", "working_turn_id": "231ba8ad-8e1b-4e45-b48f-b80b982446eb"}, "recipient": "all", "status": "finished_successfully", "update_time": 1789364705.047065, "weight": 1}, {"author": {"metadata": {}, "name": null, "role": "assistant"}, "channel": null, "content": {"content": "Worked for 13s", "content_type": "reasoning_recap"}, "create_time": 1789364698.072288, "end_turn": false, "id": "b3a06a5f-4938-4c0e-8fdf-fba284faaeeb", "metadata": {"can_save": false, "conversation_followup_suggestions_eligible": true, "cot_version": "v5", "default_model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "finished_duration_sec": 13, "hide_inline_actions": true, "message_type": "next", "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "model_switcher_deny": [], "parent_id": "27c9